[E0325] Error: `String` owns memory, but `T` must be `copy`
   ╭─[ err/544_copies_of_what_owns_memory/main.wip:7:17 ]
   │
 7 │     val count = names.copies().count()
   │                 ───────┬──────
   │                        ╰──────── owns memory
   │
   │ Help: `copies()` copies each element out; `forwards()` lends each where it lies, for any element
   │
   │ Note: a `copy` type is plain data, read without `move`: it holds no `own`, directly or in its fields
